@fact grisk.lender
# en: A goblin moneylender in a velvet waistcoat: sixty crowns today, twelve a month for six months.
text [023206] = 穿天鹅绒马甲的地精放贷人：今天六十克朗，之后六个月每月十二。

@fact grisk.ledger
# en: He calls debts "friendships", and keeps all of them in one ledger he never lets out of reach.
text [fa5464] = 他把债叫作“交情”，全都记在一本从不离手的账簿里。
# en: Pass the time of day with him.
hint [60fc73] = 跟他寒暄几句。

@fact grisk.favours
# en: He sometimes asks for favours instead of coin, and the favours are for clients he never names.
text [a745d9] = 他有时要人情而不要钱，而那些人情是替他从不透露姓名的客户讨的。
# en: He doesn't always want coin.
hint [15f768] = 他想要的，并不总是钱。

@fact grisk.newt_table
# en: He keeps the corner table at the Gilded Newt, and talks about money the way other people talk about weather: which shops are in trouble, and why.
text [797581] = 他占着镀金蝾螈酒馆角落的那张桌子，谈起钱来就像别人谈天气：哪些铺子要撑不住了，为什么。
# en: Sit with him at the Newt more than once.
hint [64043e] = 在蝾螈酒馆多陪他坐几次。

@fact grisk.collectors
# en: When a debt runs late, two trolls in waistcoats come to collect. They are polite, and very thorough.
text [ee77c7] = 债一拖欠，就会有两个穿马甲的巨魔上门收账。他们很有礼貌，也非常彻底。
# en: Fall behind on a payment.
hint [17b5fe] = 拖欠一次还款。

@fact grisk.parcels
# en: He runs parcels in oilcloth from the boathouse jetty at midnight to a cobbler's back door in the village. Nobody opens them.
text [954837] = 他在午夜把油布包着的包裹从船屋栈桥运到村里一个鞋匠的后门。从没人打开过。
# en: He has work that only happens at midnight.
hint [780f7e] = 他有些活儿只在午夜干。

@fact grisk.elixirs
# en: He deals Brightwater and Owl's Ink at the boathouse at midnight, for coin or for favours, and his price climbs before finals and for anyone who can't do without.
text [0083c4] = 他在午夜的船屋贩卖亮泉水和枭墨，收钱也收人情；期末考前，或者对离不开它的人，他的价钱就会往上涨。
# en: He sells more than loans.
hint [99022a] = 他卖的不只是借款。
